### Paragraph Structure

Each paragraph object (from paragraph-builder.js):
```javascript
{
  title: "Section Title",
  type: "info|warning|danger|table|list|compliance|requirements",
  content: "text" | { complex object },
  timestamp: "ISO date"
}
```

### Document Types

- **fire-report**: Compliance-focused paragraphs (what was assessed, results, status)
- **requirements-document**: Requirements-focused paragraphs (what must be provided, design criteria)

For initial implementation, default to `'fire-report'` since that's what users need first.

## Implementation Details

### 1. Report Builder (NEW FILE)

**File**: `api/report-builder.js`

**Purpose**: Orchestrates paragraph generation from all processors in correct order

**Structure**:
```javascript
function buildReport(projectModel, documentType = 'fire-report') {
  const paragraphs = [];

  // Generate paragraphs in report order
  // Each processor's generator returns an array of paragraph objects

  if (projectModel.hazardousSubstancesData) {
    const hazSubsParagraphs = generateHazardousSubstancesParagraphs(
      projectModel,
      documentType
    );
    paragraphs.push(...hazSubsParagraphs);
  }

  // Fire safety systems (project-level and per firecell)
  const fssSystemsParagraphs = generateFireSafetySystemsParagraphs(
    projectModel,
    documentType
  );
  paragraphs.push(...fssSystemsParagraphs);

  // Occupant load (per firecell)
  const occupantParagraphs = generateOccupantLoadParagraphs(
    projectModel,
    documentType
  );
  paragraphs.push(...occupantParagraphs);

  // Firecells (per firecell)
  const firecellParagraphs = generateFirecellsParagraphs(
    projectModel,
    documentType
  );
  paragraphs.push(...firecellParagraphs);

  // Fire resistance (project-level)
  if (projectModel.fireResistanceCalculations) {
    const fireResParagraphs = generateFireResistanceParagraphs(
      projectModel,
      projectModel.fireResistanceCalculations,
      documentType
    );
    paragraphs.push(...fireResParagraphs);
  }

  projectModel.reportParagraphs = paragraphs;
  return projectModel;
}
```

**Key Points**:
- Conditional generation based on what data exists
- Maintains report order
- Each generator is independent
- Stores final array in `projectModel.reportParagraphs`

