## Critical Design Decisions

### 1. Document Type
- Default to `'fire-report'` for initial implementation
- Add document type selection later if needed
- Easy to extend to requirements-document once pattern established

### 2. Generator Structure
- Each generator returns array of paragraphs
- Generators access full projectModel (not just their processor's data)
- Enables cross-referencing between sections

### 3. Calculation vs Presentation Separation
- Keep processors focused on calculations
- Report builder handles presentation
- Generators are pure functions (no side effects)

### 4. Paragraph Order
Order in report builder defines final report structure:
1. Hazardous Substances (project-level warning if applicable)
2. Fire Safety Systems (project-level + per firecell)
3. Occupant Load (per firecell)
4. Firecells (per firecell summaries)
5. Fire Resistance (project-level)

This order follows logical compliance assessment flow.

### 5. Data Already Exists
- All calculation data is already in projectModel
- Generators just format existing data into paragraphs
- No new calculations needed

